      "title": {
        "en": "Clean coats and tailored styling"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners frequently highlight neat, even scissor work on cavapoos and doodles, noting that coats come home smelling fresh, thoroughly brushed, and cleanly washed. Although one owner reported an accidental grooming laceration, the vast majority of clients praise the salon styling and hygiene work."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 8,
      "title": {
        "en": "Gentle handling despite rare injury reports"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Most reviewers emphasise that their dogs feel relaxed and happy during regular baths and nail trims, with staff greeting pets warmly by name. However, two critical accounts express deep concern over rough handling and injuries, including a comb snag on tangled fur and a persistent bleeding clipper cut."
      }
    }
